<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<section xml:id="sec_angle_and_dist">
        <title>Distance and Angle</title>
        <p>
                Recall that distance travelled around a circle and the angle travelled are related in a very simple way when we measure the angle in radians.
        </p>
        <exercise xml:id='exer_dist_from_angle'>
                <title>Finding Distances from Angles</title>
                <introduction>
                        <figure xml:id='fig_carousel'>
                                <caption>A Circle Representing a Carousel</caption>
                                <image width="50%">
                                        <latex-image>
                                                \begin{tikzpicture}
                                                [scale=0.7]
                                                %[scale=0.25mm]
                                                \coordinate (C) at (0,0);
                                                \coordinate (R) at (7,0);
                                                \coordinate (M) at (30:7);
                                                \fill (C) circle (0.1);
                                                \draw (C) circle (7);
                                                \draw[-stealth,dashed] (C) -- node[midway,above left]{\(7\)m} (M);
                                                \draw[-stealth] (3,0)
                                                        arc[start angle=0, end angle=30, radius=3]
                                                        node[midway,right] {\(\theta\)}
                                                ;
                                                \draw (-8,0) -- (8,0) (0,-8) -- (0,8);
                                                \foreach \a in {30, 40, ..., 380}
                                                {
                                                \begin{scope}[rotate=\a]
                                                \draw (7,-0.3625) rectangle (7.2,0.3625);
                                                \end{scope}
                                                %        \draw (\a:7) circle (0.1);
                                                }
                                                \end{tikzpicture}
                                        </latex-image>
                                </image>
                        </figure>
                        <p>
                                        A person is riding on a carousel that has a radius of <m>7</m>m. We place our coordinates axes so that they begin at the point <m>(7,0)</m>.
                        </p>
                </introduction>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                        When they have travelled through an angle of <m>\theta=1</m><nbsp/>radian, what distance along the circumference of the carousel have they travelled?
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                        When they have travelled through an angle of <m>\theta=3</m><nbsp/>radians, what distance along the circumference of the carousel have they travelled?
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                        Write a formula for the distance, <m>d</m> travelled along the circumference of the carousel when they have travelled through an angle of <m>\theta</m><nbsp/>radians.
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                                Repeat the previous questions for a carousel whose radius is <m>9</m>m.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                        Based on your results, write a formula for the distance, <m>d</m> travelled along the circumference of a circle of radius <m>r</m> when they have travelled through an angle of <m>\theta</m><nbsp/>radians.
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                </task>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id='exer_angle_from_dist'>
                <title>Finding Angles from Distances</title>
                <introduction>
                        <p>
                                        We will look again at person riding on a carousel that has a radius of <m>7</m>m.
                        </p>
                </introduction>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                        When they have travelled 
                                        <m>14</m>m along the circumference of the carousel
                                        through what angle of <m>\theta</m> (in radians)
                                        have they travelled?
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                        When they have travelled 
                                        <m>35</m>m along the circumference of the carousel
                                        through what angle of <m>\theta</m> (in radians)
                                        have they travelled?
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                        Write a formula to find 
                                        the angle <m>\theta</m> (in radians)
                                        they have travelled
                                        when 
                                        they have travelled
                                        <m>d</m>m along the circumference of the carousel.
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                </task>
                <task>
                        <statement>
                                <p>
                                        Write a formula to find 
                                        the angle <m>\theta</m> (in radians)
                                        they have travelled
                                        when 
                                        they have travelled
                                        <m>d</m>m along the circumference of a circle with radius <m>r</m>.
                                </p>
                        </statement>
                </task>
        </exercise>
</section>
